---
description: Binding PokePilot architecture gate for every gameplay/runtime change.
globs:
alwaysApply: true
---

Before changing gameplay/runtime code, read @AGENTS.md and
@docs/ARCHITECTURE.md. The architecture document is a binding repository
contract, not optional guidance.

PokePilot is a multi-game runtime whose first adapter is Pokémon Red. Generic
layers own semantic lifecycle, structured outcomes, recovery policy, and
portable capabilities. Game-specific maps, RAM, dialogue, menus, story gates,
and mechanics stay game-specific.

If a requested patch does not fit that design, do not force it into the current
layer merely to make a farm run or test green. Explain the mismatch and
reshape/refactor the boundary first. Prefer a shared invariant plus the smallest
deterministic replay over a named-map/NPC/dialogue special case or full-run-only
verification.

`docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` is the single source of truth; do not invent conflicting
local rules here.
